When you've had these moments where you can wipe away some of this accumulated crust and make decisions about with discretion, which processes to keep and which to jettison. And then build something new off of that. Use that not as something you only use in the breach, but use it as a basis for a new model. Ezra, it's been a pleasure to talk with you. The book is called Abundance. I really appreciate your time.
当你经历这些时刻时，你可以抹去一些积聚的陈规陋习，并根据自由裁量权做出决定：保留哪些程序，抛弃哪些程序。然后在此基础上建立新的东西。不要把它当成只在危机时才使用的东西，而是要把它作为新模式的基础。埃扎，和您交谈非常愉快。这本书叫《丰裕》（Abundance）。非常感谢您抽出时间。

